  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "Step 1 parts were correct and are unchanged.",
   "The breakout's 6-pin header (ST, Z, Y, X, GND, VDD) plugs into breadboard columns 4-9 in the image; each jumper wire shares a column strip with its breakout pin. The image's top half (rows j-f) is the catalogue's 'b' bank (rows f-j), so the holes use 'b'. The rows chosen are approximate; only the column strip matters electrically.",
   "Pin mapping: A0=self-test (ST), A1=Z, A2=Y, A3=X, A4=GND (driven LOW in software), A5=VDD (driven HIGH in software), as in the tutorial's table and schematic. The schematic shows the same connections.",
   "The ADXL3xx breakout is modelled with catalogue type adxl335; its VCC port stands for the breakout's VDD pin.",
   "Powering the sensor from A5 as a 5 V digital output follows the tutorial; it warns that some accelerometers are 3.3 V only. The tutorial's alternative, using the 5V and GND pins directly, is not built."
  ]
 },
